    <article class="docs-prose">
      <h1 id="stage-06-rich-tasks" class="group scroll-mt-20">Stage 06: Rich tasks<a href="#stage-06-rich-tasks" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Write four tasks: <em>Installing Audacity</em>, <em>Exporting audio</em>, <em>Removing background noise</em>, and <em>Preparing to record</em>. Add prerequisites, choices, substeps, examples, results, and troubleshooting information where each task needs them.</p>
      <p>Choose elements according to their purpose. Use <code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> for a requirement that readers must meet before starting, for example, and <code>&lt;stepresult&gt;</code> for the expected result of a step.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 30 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 05 complete.</p>
      <p>Recorded diagnostic examples below come from earlier runs. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. Run the gate for your current checkout.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-installing-audacity" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: Installing Audacity<a href="#step-1-installing-audacity" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/installing-audacity.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctask id=\"installing-audacity\">\n  \u003ctitle>Installing Audacity\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Download Audacity from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003ctaskbody>\n    \u003cprereq>\n      \u003cp>You need about 250 MB of free disk space and an account that can install software.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/prereq>\n    \u003ccontext>\n      \u003cp>Audacity is available for Windows, macOS and Linux.\n      The steps differ by operating system only at the install step.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/context>\n    \u003csteps>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Download Audacity from \u003cfilepath>https://www.audacityteam.org/download/\u003c/filepath>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cp>Select the installer for your operating system.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/info>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Install it.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cchoicetable>\n          \u003cchhead>\n            \u003cchoptionhd>Operating system\u003c/choptionhd>\n            \u003cchdeschd>How to install\u003c/chdeschd>\n          \u003c/chhead>\n          \u003cchrow>\n            \u003cchoption>Windows\u003c/choption>\n            \u003cchdesc>Double-click the downloaded \u003cfilepath>.exe\u003c/filepath> file and follow the setup wizard.\n            Accept the default location, \u003cfilepath>C:\\Program Files\\Audacity\u003c/filepath>, unless you have a reason to change it.\u003c/chdesc>\n          \u003c/chrow>\n          \u003cchrow>\n            \u003cchoption>macOS\u003c/choption>\n            \u003cchdesc>Open the downloaded \u003cfilepath>.dmg\u003c/filepath> file and drag Audacity to your \u003cfilepath>Applications\u003c/filepath> folder.\u003c/chdesc>\n          \u003c/chrow>\n          \u003cchrow>\n            \u003cchoption>Linux\u003c/choption>\n            \u003cchdesc>Install from your distribution's package manager, for example \u003ccodeph>sudo apt install audacity\u003c/codeph> on Ubuntu or Debian, \u003ccodeph>sudo dnf install audacity\u003c/codeph> on Fedora.\u003c/chdesc>\n          \u003c/chrow>\n        \u003c/choicetable>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Launch Audacity.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003csubsteps>\n          \u003csubstep>\n            \u003ccmd>If Audacity asks to scan for audio plugins, click \u003cuicontrol>OK\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n            \u003cinfo>\n              \u003cp>This happens once, on first launch.\u003c/p>\n            \u003c/info>\n          \u003c/substep>\n          \u003csubstep importance=\"optional\">\n            \u003ccmd>Choose \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>Help\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Check for Updates\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade> to confirm you have the latest version.\u003c/cmd>\n          \u003c/substep>\n        \u003c/substeps>\n        \u003cstepresult>\n          \u003cp>The main window opens with an empty project.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/stepresult>\n      \u003c/step>\n    \u003c/steps>\n    \u003cresult>\n      \u003cp>Audacity is installed and ready to use.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/result>\n    \u003cpostreq>\n      \u003cp>Connect a microphone before you continue to recording.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/postreq>\n  \u003c/taskbody>\n\u003c/task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/installing-audacity.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> states what must be true before the reader starts. It goes before <code>&lt;context&gt;</code>, and output labels it "Before you begin".</li>
      <li><code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code> states what to do after the task is done. It goes after <code>&lt;result&gt;</code>, and output labels it "What to do next".</li>
      <li><code>&lt;choicetable&gt;</code> is a step whose action depends on a condition, laid out as a two-column table: <code>&lt;chhead&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;choptionhd&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;chdeschd&gt;</code> for the headings, then one <code>&lt;chrow&gt;</code> per option with <code>&lt;choption&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;chdesc&gt;</code>. It sits inside a <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> after the <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;substeps&gt;</code> breaks a step into <code>&lt;substep&gt;</code> elements, each with its own <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code> and optional <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>. Substeps do not nest further; if they would, the step is a separate task.</li>
      <li><code>@importance="optional"</code> on a <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;substep&gt;</code> marks it as one the reader may skip. Output prefixes it with "Optional:".</li>
      <li><code>&lt;stepresult&gt;</code> says what happens after one step, as distinct from <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> for the whole task.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;codeph&gt;</code> is inline code: the <code>apt</code> command inside a sentence.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-exporting-audio" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: Exporting audio<a href="#step-2-exporting-audio" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/exporting-audio.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctask id=\"exporting-audio\">\n  \u003ctitle>Exporting audio\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Export a finished project as a WAV, MP3, OGG or FLAC file that other programs and devices can play.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003ctaskbody>\n    \u003cprereq>\n      \u003cp>Finish editing and save the project.\n      A project file (\u003cfilepath>.aup3\u003c/filepath>) can only be opened by Audacity; exporting creates an ordinary audio file.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/prereq>\n    \u003csteps>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Choose \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>File\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Export Audio\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cstepresult>\n          \u003cp>The \u003cwintitle>Export Audio\u003c/wintitle> dialog opens.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/stepresult>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Choose a format.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cchoices>\n          \u003cchoice>Choose \u003cuicontrol>WAV\u003c/uicontrol> or \u003cuicontrol>FLAC\u003c/uicontrol> for an archive copy with no quality loss.\u003c/choice>\n          \u003cchoice>Choose \u003cuicontrol>MP3\u003c/uicontrol> or \u003cuicontrol>OGG\u003c/uicontrol> for a small file to share.\u003c/choice>\n        \u003c/choices>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Set the format options.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cp>For MP3, the bit rate controls the trade-off between size and quality.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/info>\n        \u003cstepxmp>\n          \u003cp>A spoken-word podcast exports well at \u003cuicontrol>128 kbps\u003c/uicontrol>, \u003cuicontrol>Mono\u003c/uicontrol>.\n          Music needs \u003cuicontrol>192 kbps\u003c/uicontrol> or more, \u003cuicontrol>Stereo\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/stepxmp>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Choose a folder and a file name, then click \u003cuicontrol>Export\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003csteptroubleshooting>\n          \u003cp>If the \u003cuicontrol>Export\u003c/uicontrol> button is disabled, the file name is empty or the folder is read-only.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/steptroubleshooting>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep importance=\"optional\">\n        \u003ccmd>Fill in the \u003cwintitle>Edit Metadata Tags\u003c/wintitle> dialog and click \u003cuicontrol>OK\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cp>Title, artist and album are shown by most players.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/info>\n      \u003c/step>\n    \u003c/steps>\n    \u003cresult>\n      \u003cp>The exported file is in the folder you chose.\n      The project itself is unchanged.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/result>\n    \u003cexample>\n      \u003ctitle>Exporting a podcast episode\u003c/title>\n      \u003cp>Choose \u003cuicontrol>MP3\u003c/uicontrol>, set \u003cuicontrol>Bit Rate Mode\u003c/uicontrol> to \u003cuicontrol>Constant\u003c/uicontrol>, \u003cuicontrol>Quality\u003c/uicontrol> to \u003cuicontrol>128 kbps\u003c/uicontrol> and \u003cuicontrol>Channel Mode\u003c/uicontrol> to \u003cuicontrol>Force export to mono\u003c/uicontrol>.\n      A 30-minute episode exports to a file of about 27 MB.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/example>\n  \u003c/taskbody>\n\u003c/task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/exporting-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;choices&gt;</code> is the simpler alternative to <code>&lt;choicetable&gt;</code>: a list of <code>&lt;choice&gt;</code> elements, each one option, when no description column is needed.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;stepxmp&gt;</code> is an example for one step: what the settings look like in a concrete case.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code> says what to do if the step does not produce the expected result. It comes last in the step.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;example&gt;</code> is an example for the whole task, with its own <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>. It sits after <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> in the task body.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-removing-background-noise" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: Removing background noise<a href="#step-3-removing-background-noise" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/removing-background-noise.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctask id=\"removing-background-noise\">\n  \u003ctitle>Removing background noise\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Take a noise profile from a quiet section, then apply Noise Reduction to the whole track to remove hum, hiss and fan noise.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003ctaskbody>\n    \u003ccontext>\n      \u003cp>Background noise such as hum from electronics, hiss from a microphone or fan noise degrades a recording.\n      The Noise Reduction effect learns what the noise sounds like from a section that contains nothing else, then removes it everywhere.\u003c/p>\n      \u003cnote type=\"warning\">This effect changes the audio data.\n      Save the project first; you can undo with \u003cuicontrol>Ctrl+Z\u003c/uicontrol> (Windows and Linux) or \u003cuicontrol>Cmd+Z\u003c/uicontrol> (macOS).\u003c/note>\n    \u003c/context>\n    \u003csteps>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Find a section of the recording that contains only the background noise.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cp>Look for a quiet gap at the beginning or end.\n          You need at least half a second of noise-only audio.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/info>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Select that section by clicking and dragging in the waveform.\u003c/cmd>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Choose \u003cmenucascade>\u003cuicontrol>Effect\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Noise Removal and Repair\u003c/uicontrol>\u003cuicontrol>Noise Reduction\u003c/uicontrol>\u003c/menucascade>, then click \u003cuicontrol>Get Noise Profile\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cstepresult>\n          \u003cp>Audacity captures the character of the noise and closes the dialog.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/stepresult>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Select the whole track with \u003cuicontrol>Ctrl+A\u003c/uicontrol> or \u003cuicontrol>Cmd+A\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Open \u003cuicontrol>Noise Reduction\u003c/uicontrol> again, adjust the settings and click \u003cuicontrol>OK\u003c/uicontrol>.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cp>Recommended starting settings:\u003c/p>\n          \u003cul>\n            \u003cli>Noise reduction: 12 dB\u003c/li>\n            \u003cli>Sensitivity: 6\u003c/li>\n            \u003cli>Frequency smoothing: 3\u003c/li>\n          \u003c/ul>\n          \u003cnote type=\"caution\">Too much noise reduction makes voices sound metallic or underwater.\n          Start moderate, increase gradually, and use \u003cuicontrol>Preview\u003c/uicontrol> before applying.\u003c/note>\n        \u003c/info>\n      \u003c/step>\n    \u003c/steps>\n    \u003cresult>\n      \u003cp>The background noise is reduced across the whole track.\n      Play it back to check that the voice still sounds natural.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/result>\n    \u003ctasktroubleshooting>\n      \u003cp>If the voice sounds hollow after the effect, undo, then lower \u003cuicontrol>Noise reduction\u003c/uicontrol> to 6 dB and try again.\n      If the noise is a constant hum at one pitch, the \u003cuicontrol>Notch Filter\u003c/uicontrol> effect removes it with less damage to the voice.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/tasktroubleshooting>\n  \u003c/taskbody>\n\u003c/task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/removing-background-noise.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;tasktroubleshooting&gt;</code> is the task-level counterpart of <code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code>: what to do when the whole task did not give the expected result. It comes after <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> and before <code>&lt;example&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;note type="caution"&gt;</code> inside a step's <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>, beside the <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> of settings: a note can share <code>&lt;info&gt;</code> with other blocks.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-preparing-to-record" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: Preparing to record<a href="#step-4-preparing-to-record" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Create </strong><strong><code>topics/preparing-to-record.dita</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN\" \"task.dtd\">\n\n\u003ctask id=\"preparing-to-record\">\n  \u003ctitle>Preparing to record\u003c/title>\n  \u003cshortdesc>Checks to make in any order before you press Record: input level, sample rate and disk space.\u003c/shortdesc>\n  \u003ctaskbody>\n    \u003ccontext>\n      \u003cp>None of these checks depends on another, so do them in whatever order suits you.\u003c/p>\n    \u003c/context>\n    \u003csteps-unordered>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Speak at normal volume and watch the recording meter; aim for peaks around -12 dB.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003ctutorialinfo>\n          \u003cp>Leaving headroom avoids clipping, the flat-topped distortion that no effect can repair.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/tutorialinfo>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Set the project sample rate to 44,100 Hz in the bottom-left corner of the window.\u003c/cmd>\n      \u003c/step>\n      \u003cstep>\n        \u003ccmd>Check that the drive holding the project has at least 1 GB free.\u003c/cmd>\n        \u003cinfo>\n          \u003cp>An hour of stereo audio at 44,100 Hz and 32-bit float needs about 1.2 GB.\u003c/p>\n        \u003c/info>\n      \u003c/step>\n    \u003c/steps-unordered>\n  \u003c/taskbody>\n\u003c/task>"} lang="xml" title="topics/preparing-to-record.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the new elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> replaces <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code> when the order does not matter. The children are still <code>&lt;step&gt;</code> elements; output renders them as a bulleted rather than numbered list. Say in the <code>&lt;context&gt;</code> that the order is free, as this topic does.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;tutorialinfo&gt;</code> is additional information for a reader who is learning, as opposed to <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>, which is for anyone doing the step. A stylesheet for expert readers can drop it.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-5-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 5: Update the README and run the gate<a href="#step-5-update-the-readme-and-run-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 05: inline and block.\n+You are on stage 06: rich tasks.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n9 file(s): 9 valid, 0 invalid.\n…\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>The order inside <code>&lt;taskbody&gt;</code> is fixed: <code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;context&gt;</code>, then <code>&lt;steps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;result&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tasktroubleshooting&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;example&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code>. To see the validator hold that order, move the <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code> in <em>Installing Audacity</em> above <code>&lt;result&gt;</code> and run the gate.</p>
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="publish-your-changes" class="group scroll-mt-20">Publish your changes<a href="#publish-your-changes" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <p>Add the lesson's topics to <code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code>, then rebuild the guide. The complete map at this checkpoint is:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"\u003c?xml version=\"1.0\" encoding=\"UTF-8\"?>\n\u003c!DOCTYPE map PUBLIC \"-//OASIS//DTD DITA Map//EN\" \"map.dtd\">\n\n\u003cmap>\n  \u003ctitle>Audio user guide\u003c/title>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/exporting-audio.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/installing-audacity.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/preparing-to-record.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/removing-background-noise.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/trimming-audio.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-audacity.dita\"/>\n  \u003ctopicref href=\"topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\"/>\n\u003c/map>"} lang="xml" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      <CodeBlock code={"dita --project=project.json --output=out\npython3 scripts/check-output-links.py out"} lang="bash" />
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li>Before and after: <code>&lt;prereq&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>Inside a step: <code>&lt;cmd&gt;</code> first; then <code>&lt;info&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tutorialinfo&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;substeps&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;choices&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;choicetable&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;stepxmp&gt;</code> in any order; then <code>&lt;stepresult&gt;</code>, then <code>&lt;steptroubleshooting&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li>After the steps, in order: <code>&lt;result&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tasktroubleshooting&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;example&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;postreq&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;steps-unordered&gt;</code> for checks in any order; <code>@importance="optional"</code> for steps that can be skipped.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;tutorialinfo&gt;</code> for the learner, <code>&lt;info&gt;</code> for everyone.</li>
      </ul>
